    "content": "# Murudeshwar Scuba Diving: The Complete 2026 Guide\n\nScuba diving in Murudeshwar means diving at **Netrani Island**, a rocky coral island about **19 km off the Murudeshwar coast** in the Arabian Sea. You don't dive at the temple beach itself. You board a boat at Murudeshwar, cruise for about an hour, and dive on Netrani's reef with a certified instructor beside you.\n\nThis guide covers what a dive day looks like, what it costs, who can dive, and when to go.\n\n## Quick facts\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| Dive site | Netrani Island (also called Pigeon Island) |\n| Distance from Murudeshwar | About 19 km by boat |\n| Boat ride | 60–75 minutes each way |\n| Packages | ₹3,500 (30–40 min dive) and ₹4,500 (45–55 min dive) per person |\n| Age limit | 10 to 60 years, medically fit |\n| Swimming needed? | No |\n| Season | October to May |\n| Daily timings | 8:00 AM – 3:00 PM |\n| Booking advance | ₹500 per person |\n\n## Do you need to know swimming?\n\nNo. Scuba diving is not swimming. You wear a BCD (buoyancy jacket) that keeps you afloat on the surface, and underwater you breathe through a regulator. Your instructor holds your harness and controls your depth, buoyancy and direction the whole time. Your job is to relax and breathe slowly.\n\nIf you can't swim, read our [non-swimmers guide](/blog/scuba-diving-murudeshwar-non-swimmers) before you come.\n\n## Murudeshwar scuba diving price\n\nThere are two packages, and both include the same things. The difference is how long you stay underwater.\n\n| Package | Dive time | Price per person |\n|---|---|---|\n| Full Netrani Dive | 30–40 minutes, up to about 12 m | ₹3,500 |\n| Extended Deep Dive | 45–55 minutes | ₹4,500 |\n\n**Both packages include:**\n- The return boat trip from Murudeshwar to Netrani Island\n- A 1:1 certified instructor\n- All equipment (wetsuit, mask, fins, BCD, regulator, cylinder)\n- Surface snorkelling gear while you wait on the boat\n- Refreshments\n- Free underwater HD photos and videos, transferred to your phone the same day\n\nFor a full breakdown, see the [Murudeshwar scuba diving price guide](/blog/murudeshwar-scuba-diving-price-cost).\n\n## What a dive day looks like\n\n![Murudeshwar scuba dive boat departure with gear and guests|Murudeshwar harbour boat departure for the morning crossing to Netrani Island](/images/blog/murudeshwar-dive-boat-departure.jpg)\n\n\n\n| Time | What happens |\n|---|---|\n| 8:00 – 8:30 AM | Report at the dive desk on Temple Main Road. Check-in, medical declaration, gear fitting. |\n| 8:30 – 9:45 AM | Boat ride to Netrani past the Shiva statue. Dolphins are often seen on the way. |\n| 9:45 – 10:15 AM | Breathing practice and hand signals in Netrani's sheltered bay. |\n| 10:15 AM – 1:30 PM | Dives run in turns. While others dive, you can snorkel or rest on the boat. |\n| 1:30 – 2:30 PM | Boat ride back to Murudeshwar. |\n| 2:30 – 3:00 PM | Photos and videos sent to your phone. |\n\nPlan for the whole morning and early afternoon. Don't book a bus or train before 3:30 PM. For more detail, see [scuba diving timings](/blog/scuba-diving-timings).\n\n## What you'll see underwater\n\n![Scuba diver underwater face-to-face with coral reef fish at Netrani|Netrani Island coral reef: Diving 10 to 12 metres down alongside vibrant marine life](/images/blog/netrani-coral-reef-fish.jpg)\n\n\n\nNetrani's reef sits around rocky pinnacles. Common sightings include:\n- parrotfish, butterflyfish, angelfish and clownfish\n- triggerfish\n- honeycomb moray eels\n- schools of barracuda\n- stingrays, now and then\n\nSea turtles and reef sharks show up occasionally, but sightings are never guaranteed. Our [Netrani marine life guide](/blog/netrani-island-marine-life) covers what lives there.\n\n## Who can dive?\n\n- **Age:** 10 to 60 years. Children under 10 can come on the boat with a parent and snorkel at the surface, but they cannot scuba dive.\n- **Health:** You should be medically fit. Tell us before booking if you have heart conditions, uncontrolled blood pressure, epilepsy, asthma, recent surgery, or are pregnant. You'll fill a medical declaration on the morning of the dive.\n- **Glasses:** Spectacles can't be worn inside a mask. Soft contact lenses are fine.\n\nThe full rules are in our [scuba diving age limit guide](/blog/scuba-diving-age-limit).\n\n## When to go\n\nDiving runs **October to May**. Boats don't go out during the monsoon (roughly June to September) because the sea is too rough.\n\nThe calmest seas and clearest water are usually found from around November to March. Visibility changes day to day with weather and currents. If the port authorities issue a weather alert or the sea is unsafe, the trip is cancelled and you get a full refund or a free reschedule.\n\nSee [the best time for scuba diving in Murudeshwar](/blog/best-time-scuba-diving-murudeshwar).\n\n## How to book\n\n1. Call **+91 78299 75777** or WhatsApp **+91 74063 29777** with your date, the number of divers and their ages.\n2. Pay the **₹500 per person advance** to hold your boat seat and instructor.\n3. Pay the balance in cash or UPI at check-in on the dive morning.\n\n**Cancellation:** if you cancel 48 hours or more before the dive date, you get a full refund of the advance. Cancellations within 48 hours, and no-shows, lose the advance. Slots are limited each day to keep it 1:1, so weekends and holidays fill early.\n\nFor a step-by-step version, read [how to book Netrani scuba diving](/blog/netrani-island-scuba-diving-booking-how-to-book).\n\n## Getting to Murudeshwar\n\n- **Train:** Murudeshwar Railway Station (code MRDW) is on the Konkan Railway line, about 3 km from the temple and beach.\n- **Bus:** Overnight buses from Bengaluru take 9–10 hours. Buses from Mangaluru take about 3 hours.\n- **Air:** The nearest airport is Mangaluru (IXE), about 160 km away.\n\nFull directions are in [how to reach Murudeshwar](/how-to-reach-murudeshwar).\n\n## What to bring\n\n- Swimwear to wear under the wetsuit\n- A towel and a change of clothes\n- Sunscreen and a cap\n- A light breakfast. Don't dive on an empty stomach, and don't eat a heavy meal either.\n- Seasickness tablets if you get motion sick. Take them 30–60 minutes before the boat leaves.\n- A waterproof pouch for your phone\n\nSee the [what to bring checklist](/blog/what-to-bring-scuba-diving-murudeshwar).\n\n## FAQs\n\n**Is Murudeshwar scuba diving safe for beginners?**\nYes. Every beginner dives with their own certified instructor, after a briefing and shallow-water practice. The instructor stays in contact with you for the whole dive.\n\n**Can couples or friends dive together?**\nYes. Each of you has your own instructor, and you dive at the same time.\n\n**Is scuba diving done at Murudeshwar beach?**\nNo. The dives happen at Netrani Island, about 19 km out by boat.\n\n**Are photos really free?**\nYes. Underwater photos and videos are included in both packages and sent to your phone the same day.\n\n---\n\n**Ready to dive?** Call +91 78299 75777 or WhatsApp +91 74063 29777 to check slots for your date.\n\n👉\n"
