    "content": "# Netrani Island Scuba Diving: What to Expect\n\nNetrani Island is the best-known scuba diving site on the Karnataka coast. It is a small, uninhabited rocky island about 19 km off Murudeshwar in the Arabian Sea. Its reef draws first-time divers from Bengaluru, Goa, Mangaluru and beyond.\n\nThis page covers the dive itself: the island, the reef, what you'll see, and how your time underwater actually goes.\n\n## About Netrani Island\n\n- **Location:** about 19 km off Murudeshwar, Uttara Kannada district, Karnataka\n- **Also called:** Pigeon Island, after the pigeons that nest on it\n- **Shape:** a heart-shaped rocky island with steep sides that drop into the sea\n- **On land:** no residents, and visitors don't land on the island. All diving is done from the boat.\n\nThe rocky walls and pinnacles around the island make a good home for reef fish. Away from the mainland, the water is usually much clearer than near the beach.\n\n## The reef and what you'll see\n\nThe standard dive goes down to about **12 metres**, along the rocks and coral patches. Here's what you might see:\n\n| What | How often |\n|---|---|\n| Parrotfish, butterflyfish, angelfish, triggerfish | Most dives |\n| Clownfish in anemones | Often |\n| Schools of small reef fish and barracuda | Often |\n| Honeycomb moray eels hiding in the rocks | Sometimes |\n| Stingrays | Sometimes |\n| Sea turtles, reef sharks | Occasionally, not guaranteed |\n| Dolphins (from the boat, on the way) | Frequently |\n\nFor more on what lives there, read the [Netrani Island marine life guide](/blog/netrani-island-marine-life).\n\n## How the dive works for a beginner\n\n1. **Briefing on shore.** You learn how to breathe through the regulator, how to clear your mask and how to equalise your ears, plus the basic hand signals: OK, problem, up, and ear trouble.\n2. **Boat ride.** About 60–75 minutes from Murudeshwar to Netrani.\n3. **Gearing up.** Your instructor fits your BCD jacket, cylinder and mask.\n4. **Surface practice.** In Netrani's sheltered bay you breathe with your face in the water until you feel relaxed.\n5. **Descent.** You go down slowly, equalising your ears as you go. Your instructor holds your harness throughout.\n6. **The dive.** 30–40 minutes, or 45–55 minutes on the extended package. Your instructor controls depth and direction and takes your photos and videos.\n7. **Ascent and back to the boat.** You can snorkel at the surface while others take their turn.\n\nIf you feel uncomfortable at any point, give the \"up\" signal and your instructor brings you up. You are never left alone underwater.\n\n## Netrani Island scuba diving price\n\n| Package | Dive time | Price |\n|---|---|---|\n| Full Netrani Dive | 30–40 min | ₹3,500 per person |\n| Extended Deep Dive | 45–55 min | ₹4,500 per person |\n\nBoth include the boat, a 1:1 instructor, all gear, refreshments and free photos and videos. The full breakdown is in our [price guide](/blog/murudeshwar-scuba-diving-price-cost).\n\n## Best time to dive at Netrani\n\nDiving runs from **October to May**. The monsoon months, roughly June to September, are closed because the sea is rough.\n\nClear, calm days are most common in the middle of the season. Conditions still change daily, so no month guarantees perfect visibility. If the authorities issue a weather alert, the trip is cancelled and you get a full refund or a free reschedule.\n\nSee [the best time for scuba diving in Murudeshwar](/blog/best-time-scuba-diving-murudeshwar).\n\n## Scuba vs snorkelling at Netrani\n\nSnorkelling keeps you at the surface looking down. Scuba takes you down to the reef, where you see the fish at eye level. Snorkelling gear is included with our scuba packages, so you can do both. If you're deciding between them, read [scuba diving vs snorkelling at Netrani](/blog/scuba-diving-vs-snorkelling-netrani-island).\n\n## Who can dive at Netrani?\n\n- **Age:** 10 to 60 years\n- **Swimming:** not needed\n- **Health:** medically fit. You'll fill a declaration on the morning of the dive.\n\nRead the [age limit and medical rules](/blog/scuba-diving-age-limit).\n\n## Tips for a better Netrani dive\n\n- **Eat a light breakfast.** Not too heavy, and not nothing.\n- **Take seasickness tablets** before the boat ride if you're prone to motion sickness.\n- **Equalise early and often** as you go down. Never force it.\n- **Breathe slowly and deeply.** It calms you and makes your air last longer.\n- **Don't touch the coral or the animals.** It protects the reef, and it protects you.\n\n## FAQs\n\n**How deep is the Netrani dive?**\nThe standard beginner dive goes to about 12 metres.\n\n**Can I land on Netrani Island?**\nNo. Diving and snorkelling are done from the boat.\n\n**Is Netrani better than diving in Goa?**\nNetrani is further offshore, so its water is often clearer than the near-shore sites. Conditions vary daily everywhere. See our guide for [divers coming from Goa](/blog/goa-to-murudeshwar-scuba-diving).\n\n---\n\nTo book Netrani scuba diving, call **+91 78299 75777** or WhatsApp **+91 74063 29777**.\n\n👉\n"
