    "content": "# Bangalore to Netrani Island: How to Plan a Scuba Weekend\n\nNetrani Island is one of the closest coral reef dive sites to Bengaluru. You can do it as a weekend trip: travel overnight on Friday, dive on Saturday, and be home by Sunday.\n\n## Bangalore to Netrani Island distance\n\n| Leg | Distance | Time |\n|---|---|---|\n| Bengaluru → Murudeshwar (road) | About 480–500 km | 9–10 hours by bus or car |\n| Murudeshwar → Netrani Island (boat) | About 19 km | 60–75 minutes |\n\nThere's no direct road to Netrani, because it's an island. You travel to Murudeshwar first and take the dive boat from there.\n\n## Option 1: Overnight bus (most popular)\n\n- KSRTC and private sleeper buses run every night from Bengaluru to Murudeshwar and Bhatkal.\n- The journey takes about **9–10 hours**. A 9–10 PM departure reaches Murudeshwar early the next morning.\n- Buses drop you at **Murudeshwar Highway Cross**. From there an auto takes under 5 minutes to the beach.\n\n**Tip:** book a sleeper bus. You need to be rested to dive.\n\n## Option 2: Train\n\nMurudeshwar has its own station, **MRDW**, on the Konkan Railway, about 3 km from the beach. There's an overnight train connection from Bengaluru via Mangaluru. Check current timings and availability on IRCTC before you plan. Autos are available at the station.\n\n## Option 3: Drive\n\nThe usual route goes via Tumakuru and Shivamogga towards the coast, then joins NH 66 to Murudeshwar. Allow 9–10 hours with breaks. The ghat sections are slow at night. Parking is available at the temple parking area, about a 2-minute walk from our dive desk.\n\n## 2-day weekend plan\n\n**Friday night**\n- Take an overnight bus or train from Bengaluru, around 9–10 PM.\n\n**Saturday: dive day**\n| Time | Plan |\n|---|---|\n| Early morning | Reach Murudeshwar, check into a hotel, freshen up, eat a light breakfast |\n| 8:00 AM | Report at our dive desk on Temple Main Road |\n| 8:30 AM | Boat leaves for Netrani Island |\n| Late morning | Your scuba dive (30–40 or 45–55 minutes) |\n| 2:30–3:00 PM | Back on shore, photos and videos sent to your phone |\n| Evening | Visit Murudeshwar temple and the Shiva statue, then the beach at sunset |\n\n**Sunday**\n- Morning options: Bhatkal, or a drive to Gokarna or Jog Falls (season permitting), then an evening bus back to Bengaluru.\n- Or take Saturday night's bus and be home on Sunday morning.\n\nFor a longer trip, see the [Bangalore to Murudeshwar travel guide](/blog/bangalore-to-murudeshwar-travel-guide).\n\n## Important: don't fly or drive up the ghats right after a dive\n\nDivers are generally advised not to fly within 24 hours of a dive. Large altitude changes straight after diving add a small extra risk. Bengaluru sits at about 900 m. An overnight bus that evening is fine for most try-divers, but if you plan to fly anywhere, leave a gap of at least 24 hours.\n\n## Budget estimate (per person)\n\n| Item | Approximate cost |\n|---|---|\n| Sleeper bus, both ways | Varies by operator and season. Check booking apps. |\n| Scuba dive | ₹3,500 or ₹4,500 |\n| Stay in Murudeshwar, 1 night | Varies widely |\n| Food | Varies |\n\nThe dive price includes the boat, instructor, gear and photos. See the [price guide](/blog/murudeshwar-scuba-diving-price-cost).\n\n## Coming in a big group?\n\nCollege and office groups from Bengaluru often book a tempo traveller and dive together. See our [bulk scuba booking](/bulk-scuba-booking) page for group bookings.\n\n## FAQs\n\n**Can I do Netrani as a day trip from Bangalore?**\nNot really. With 9–10 hours of travel each way, you need at least one night.\n\n**When should I book?**\nWeekends and long holidays from October to May fill early. Book a week or more ahead and pay the ₹500 advance.\n\n**What if the trip is cancelled because of the weather?**\nYou get a full refund or a free reschedule. Pick refundable or flexible bus tickets if you can.\n\n---\n\nBook your Saturday slot: call **+91 78299 75777** or WhatsApp **+91 74063 29777**.\n\n👉\n"
