    "content": "# Scuba Diving in Karnataka: Where to Go\n\nKarnataka has about 320 km of coastline, from Karwar in the north to Mangaluru in the south. But if you want a real coral reef dive, most divers end up at one place: **Netrani Island, off Murudeshwar.**\n\n## Why Netrani is Karnataka's main dive site\n\n![Scuba diver swimming with school of marine fish underwater in Karnataka|Karnataka's premier coral reef diving site at Netrani Island](/images/murudeshwara/netrani_scuba_diver_underwater.webp)\n\n\n\nMost of the Karnataka coast has sandy beaches and river mouths. That means murky water near the shore, which isn't good for diving. Netrani is different:\n- it sits about **19 km offshore**, away from river runoff\n- its **rocky walls and pinnacles** give reef life somewhere to live\n- the water is usually **much clearer** than near the beach\n\nThat's why scuba diving in Karnataka and scuba diving at Netrani are almost the same thing.\n\n## Coastal options compared\n\n| Place | What's available | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Netrani Island (from Murudeshwar)** | Boat scuba dives on a coral reef, plus snorkelling | The state's best-known reef dive. 60–75 min boat ride each way. |\n| **Karwar / Devbagh area** | Mainly water sports and snorkelling, with some shallow try-dives | Check what's offered and where the dive actually happens. |\n| **Gokarna** | Beaches and water sports | Divers from Gokarna usually travel to Murudeshwar for Netrani. See [scuba diving near Gokarna](/blog/scuba-diving-near-gokarna). |\n| **Udupi / Malpe** | Beach water sports, and boat trips to St Mary's Island | See [scuba diving near Udupi](/blog/scuba-diving-near-udupi). |\n| **Mangaluru** | City beaches | Most divers head north to Netrani. See [scuba diving near Mangalore](/blog/scuba-diving-near-mangalore). |\n\n**A word of caution:** some \"scuba\" trips along the coast are short, shallow dives near the beach, not reef dives. Always ask *where* the dive happens and *how long* you'll be underwater.\n\n## Scuba diving in Karnataka: price\n\nAt Netrani with us:\n\n| Package | Dive time | Price |\n|---|---|---|\n| Full Netrani Dive | 30–40 min | ₹3,500 |\n| Extended Deep Dive | 45–55 min | ₹4,500 |\n\nBoth include the boat, a 1:1 instructor, all gear and free photos and videos. Read the [Murudeshwar scuba diving price guide](/blog/murudeshwar-scuba-diving-price-cost), or compare with [scuba prices across India](/blog/scuba-diving-price-india).\n\n## When to dive in Karnataka\n\nThe coast follows the monsoon:\n- **October to May:** the dive season\n- **June to September:** closed. The sea is rough and boats don't run.\n\n## Who can dive?\n\n- Ages **10 to 60**\n- **No swimming** needed for a guided try-dive\n- Medically fit\n\n## Planning your Karnataka dive trip\n\n1. **Get to Murudeshwar.** It's on NH 66 and the Konkan Railway (station MRDW). See [how to reach Murudeshwar](/how-to-reach-murudeshwar).\n2. **Book a slot.** Pay the ₹500 per person advance.\n3. **Dive day.** Report at 8:00 AM. You're back by about 3:00 PM.\n4. **Add the coast.** Murudeshwar temple, Gokarna, Honnavar and Jog Falls are all close by. See [places to visit near Murudeshwar](/blog/best-places-to-visit-near-murudeshwar).\n\n## Want to get certified?\n\nA try-dive is a guided experience, not a certification. If you love it, the next step is an entry-level course like PADI Open Water Diver, which lets you dive with a buddy instead of an instructor holding you. Ask us about it.\n\n## FAQs\n\n**Which is the best place for scuba diving in Karnataka?**\nNetrani Island, reached by boat from Murudeshwar.\n\n**Is scuba diving possible in Karnataka during the monsoon?**\nNo. Dive boats don't run from about June to September.\n\n**Can beginners scuba dive in Karnataka?**\nYes. Guided try-dives at Netrani are made for first-timers and non-swimmers.\n\n---\n\nBook Karnataka's best reef dive: call **+91 78299 75777** or WhatsApp **+91 74063 29777**.\n\n👉\n"
