    "content": "# Scuba Diving Near Mangalore: Go to Netrani Island\n\nSearching for scuba diving in Mangalore? The closest proper coral reef dive is **Netrani Island**, reached by boat from **Murudeshwar**, north of Mangaluru along the coast.\n\nThe beaches around Mangaluru city are sandy, with river mouths nearby, so the water close to shore is usually too murky for good diving. Netrani sits about 19 km out at sea, where the water is clearer and the rocks support reef life.\n\n## Mangalore to Murudeshwar distance\n\n| Route | Distance | Time |\n|---|---|---|\n| Mangaluru → Murudeshwar by road (NH 66) | About 160–170 km | About 3–4 hours |\n| Murudeshwar → Netrani Island by boat | About 19 km | 60–75 minutes |\n\nOn the way north you pass Udupi, Kundapura and Bhatkal.\n\n## How to get from Mangalore to Murudeshwar\n\n**By bus**\nKSRTC and private buses run often along NH 66 from Mangaluru towards Bhatkal, Murudeshwar and Karwar. The ride is about 3 hours. Get off at **Murudeshwar Highway Cross**, then take an auto to the beach, which is under 5 minutes.\n\n**By train**\nKonkan Railway trains run from Mangaluru to **Murudeshwar station (MRDW)**, which is about 3 km from the beach. Check IRCTC for current timings. Not every train stops at MRDW.\n\n**By car or taxi**\nDrive straight up NH 66. Leave Mangaluru by about **4:30–5:00 AM** to reach our dive desk for the 8:00 AM reporting time. Parking is available at the temple parking area.\n\n**From Mangaluru airport (IXE)**\nThe airport is about 160 km from Murudeshwar. A taxi is the quickest option. If you're flying in, arrive the day before your dive.\n\n## Can I do it as a day trip from Mangalore?\n\nYes, if you leave very early.\n\n| Time | Plan |\n|---|---|\n| 4:30 AM | Leave Mangaluru by car or taxi |\n| 7:45 AM | Reach Murudeshwar and eat a light breakfast |\n| 8:00 AM | Report at our dive desk on Temple Main Road |\n| 8:30 AM – 2:30 PM | Boat to Netrani, scuba dive, snorkelling, boat back |\n| 3:00 PM | Lunch, then visit the temple and the Shiva statue |\n| 4:30 PM | Drive back. Reach Mangaluru by about 8:00 PM. |\n\nFor a relaxed trip, stay overnight in Murudeshwar the night before.\n\n## Price\n\n| Package | Dive time | Price |\n|---|---|---|\n| Full Netrani Dive | 30–40 min | ₹3,500 |\n| Extended Deep Dive | 45–55 min | ₹4,500 |\n\nBoth include the boat, a 1:1 instructor, all gear and free photos and videos. Pay a ₹500 per person advance to book. See the [price guide](/blog/murudeshwar-scuba-diving-price-cost).\n\n## What about snorkelling or water sports near Mangalore?\n\nBeaches near Mangaluru and Udupi, like Malpe, have water sports and boat trips to St Mary's Island. Those are great for sightseeing, but if you want to be underwater on a reef, Netrani is the trip to make. Read [scuba diving near Udupi](/blog/scuba-diving-near-udupi) if you're based there.\n\n## Who can dive?\n\n- Age **10 to 60**\n- **No swimming needed**\n- Medically fit. Read the [age limit and medical rules](/blog/scuba-diving-age-limit).\n\n## Best season\n\n**October to May.** Boats don't run in the monsoon, from about June to September. Weather cancellations get a full refund or a free reschedule.\n\n## FAQs\n\n**Is there scuba diving in Mangalore city?**\nFor a reef dive, most people from Mangaluru travel north to Netrani Island via Murudeshwar.\n\n**How far is Murudeshwar from Mangalore?**\nAbout 160–170 km by road, roughly 3–4 hours.\n\n**Can a group from Mangalore book together?**\nYes. College and office groups often come together. See [bulk booking](/bulk-scuba-booking).\n\n---\n\nComing from Mangaluru? Call **+91 78299 75777** or WhatsApp **+91 74063 29777** to book your slot.\n\n👉\n"
