    "content": "\n# Murudeshwar Temple Timings & Complete Travel Guide (2026)\n\nWelcome to our comprehensive guide on **Murudeshwar Temple Timings & Complete Travel Guide (2026)**.\n\nIf you are planning a scuba diving trip to **Netrani Island, Murudeshwar**, this article provides essential insights into this topic.\n\n## Key Information\n\n* **Direct Operator Support:** Call [+91 78299 75777](tel:+917829975777) for instant confirmation.\n* **Timing:** Morning reporting from 8 AM daily.\n* **Season:** October to May. Closed during monsoon.\n\n---\n\n## Murudeshwar Temple Overview & History\n\nSurrounded on three sides by the Arabian Sea atop Kanduka Hill, the Murudeshwar Temple is dedicated to Lord Shiva (Sri Mridesha Linga). According to legend from the *Ramayana*, the demon king Ravana obtained the sacred *Atma-Linga* from Lord Shiva. When tricked by Lord Ganesha to place it on the ground at Gokarna, Ravana attempted to uproot it in anger. A piece of the cloth covering the Linga was flung across the coast, landing at Kanduka Hill, which became the sacred site of Murudeshwar.\n\n---\n\n## Temple Timings & Pooja Schedule (2026)\n\n* **Morning Darshan:** 06:00 AM to 01:00 PM\n* **Temple Afternoon Break:** 01:00 PM to 03:00 PM (Sanctum closed for cleaning & rest)\n* **Evening Darshan:** 03:00 PM to 08:30 PM\n* **Maha Aarti:** 12:15 PM (Noon) and 07:30 PM (Evening)\n\n---\n\n## Must-Visit Attractions Inside the Temple Complex\n\n### 1. The 123-Foot Lord Shiva Statue\n* The second-tallest Shiva statue in the world, sculpted by master artist Kashinath and his team over two years. It is oriented so that the sun rays illuminate the deity directly throughout the day.\n\n### 2. The 249-Foot Raja Gopura (20-Storied Tower)\n* One of the tallest temple gopurams in India. It is equipped with a modern elevator (lift fee approx. ₹10 per person) taking visitors directly to the **18th floor**. Large glass viewing windows offer a breathtaking 360-degree panoramic vista of the Arabian Sea, Murudeshwar Beach, and the Shiva statue.\n\n### 3. Bhukailasa Cave Museum\n* Located directly beneath the Shiva statue, this air-conditioned cave museum showcases life-size stone and plaster sculptures depicting the mythological legend of the Atma-Linga and Ravana. (Entry fee approx. ₹20).\n\n---\n\n## Combining Temple Darshan with Scuba Diving\n\nBecause the scuba diving trip to Netrani Island runs from **8:30 AM to 2:45 PM**, you can seamlessly combine both experiences:\n* **Option A:** Take early morning temple darshan between 6:30 AM and 7:45 AM before reporting for your boat dive.\n* **Option B:** Complete your scuba dive first, return to shore at 3:00 PM, freshen up, and visit the temple and Raja Gopura lift between 4:00 PM and 6:30 PM to catch the sunset and evening Maha Aarti!\n    "
